	'k12222e34' => 'The Last Kiln',
	'k122566f9' => 'Delivery &amp; screenings',
	'k12a258fd' => 'For individual shooting assignments, consultative field work, or specialised technical delivery, we provide distinct day rates and delivery packages. Director\'s day (covering preparation or active location shooting): €1,200. Festival deliverables package (providing DCP creation and professional subtitling in two languages): €4,500. These rates apply to standalone production phases, extended festival preparation, or targeted editorial consultations requested outside standard multi-month production commissions.',
	'k13ec1b15' => 'Broadcast, 52 min',
	'k15547d01' => 'Monday to Thursday 10:00–18:00, Friday by appointment. Proposals are read every Monday and answered within five working days. Field days follow the working hours of the people in the film.',
	'k17e74ce8' => 'One letter on the first Monday of each month: a still, a field note and open months.',
	'k18f2761d' => 'Riverwatch Alliance / Short',
	'k18fd3bb6' => 'Research &amp; Access',
	'k19abed78' => 'You can reach Utsushi Films directly by emailing propose@utsushi-films.example or calling 010 482 7716. Our physical address is Studio 3, Ropewalk Yard, 12 Netmakers\' Lane, Port Alder. Studio working hours are Monday to Thursday from 10:00 to 18:00, with Friday visits arranged by appointment. During active location shooting blocks, our field days operate whenever the people in the film work, while studio administration continues as scheduled.',
	'k1a1db2bc' => 'Commissioned by Riverwatch Alliance, this 18-minute short documentary examines water quality monitoring along industrial river estuaries. Production took place across several months alongside volunteer scientists gathering early morning water samples from small boats. The film captures quiet field measurements, tidal movements, and laboratory analysis, focusing on ecological observation rather than institutional rhetoric. Delivered in 2024, What the River Carries screened directly for community audiences, environmental forums, and partner organisations associated with Riverwatch Alliance.',
