	'k3b01e10f' => 'Our documentary films are presented across festival venues, public broadcast television, and community screening spaces. This index lists confirmed broadcasts, premieres, and institutional viewings from 2021 to 2025.',
	'k3bccef48' => 'Short, 18 min',
	'k3c2151ca' => 'Keepers of the Archive is a three-part series of 26-minute episodes produced in 2021 for Meridian Arts Channel, tracking conservation specialists restoring delicate historic celluloid collections. Both projects demonstrate our continuous commitment to physical labour, material culture, and observational precision.',
	'k3c853589' => 'When you propose a film or submit an inquiry through our website or via propose@utsushi-films.example, we collect your name, email address, organisation, project description, and timeframe. This information is stored securely on private systems at Studio 3 in Port Alder and is used solely to evaluate your proposal and respond within 5 working days. We never share or sell contact information to third parties.',
	'k3f030077' => 'Field notes and dispatches from the work',
	'k3f18e8bf' => 'Priya Natarajan',
	'k3f3e9348' => 'Field Letters is our monthly production dispatch sent to commissioning editors, festival curators, and documentary collaborators. It offers quiet reflections from active shoots and notices of upcoming studio availability.',
	'k405a6c67' => 'Halden Public Television · Broadcast hour, 52 min · 2024',
	'k40b6c370' => 'Our earlier portfolio includes The Last Kiln, a 28-minute short documentary completed in 2022 that screened at the Ostmere Short Film Forum, documenting the final firing of a traditional brick kiln.',
	'k4240cbe3' => 'Editorial spans ten to sixteen weeks in Port Alder with two collaborative viewing rounds, followed by festival deliverables, broadcast mastering, and public screenings.',
	'k42504b28' => 'Propose',
	'k44345ae8' => 'A full commission provides end-to-end production directed by Ines Calder, supported by producer Tomasz Wren and our permanent studio collaborators. This includes dedicated cinematography by Adaeze Morrow, location sound recording by Luca Ferreira, research management by Priya Natarajan, editing by Hana Sørlie, and colour grading and mastering by Owen Achterberg. All equipment, insurance, location travel, archival backups, and sound mixes are fully managed under the contracted production fee.',
