	'k68f51c9d' => 'Our working routine in the field follows the rhythm of our subjects rather than standard production hours. A typical day starts at 05:30 on the quay, setting up equipment in cold dawn air before the fishing boats or dockside facilities begin their shifts. We film continuously until the work stops, staying close without directing action or prompting conversation. Nights are spent back at base, systematically cataloguing audio and video logs, backing up drives, and preparing microphones for the following dawn.',
