	'kdb9e81f6' => 'Commission rates',
	'kdbc5b37d' => 'Commissioned by Halden Public Television, Salt Hours documents the complete harvesting cycle of an artisanal salt-pan family over a six-month season. Our production team spent consecutive months beside the workers, following the daily evaporation, raking, and crystallisation under low coastal sun. The finished work is a 52-minute broadcast hour delivered in 2024 for regional and national television broadcast by Halden Public Television. The documentary avoids explanatory voiceover, allowing the ambient sound of coastal brine and manual timber tools to carry the narrative.',
	'kdcd13da0' => 'All rates exclude VAT. Deposit 30% on signing.',
	'kde0a6840' => 'Studio hours',
	'ke2d0dd8d' => 'Subscribers receive exactly one email dispatch sent on the first Monday of each month. Each letter contains three specific elements: a single unreleased production still captured during recent field work, an unhurried field note written by director Ines Calder or our crew, and an updated list of open production months for future commissions. We do not send marketing blasts, commercial promotions, or weekly announcements.',
	'ke3d221b9' => 'Commissioned by Larchmont Health Trust, Night Shift at Ward Nine explores the nocturnal operations of an acute hospital ward. Over months of preliminary research and quiet nighttime presence, the production established strict consent-led protocols with nursing staff and patients. The resulting 24-minute institutional documentary was delivered in 2023 for specialized staff training and institutional presentations at Larchmont Health Trust. By recording available desk lamp light and corridor acoustics, the film presents an intimate portrait of healthcare labour.',
	'ke4a05d8f' => 'Colourist &amp; Post',
	'ke78e596f' => 'We will not undertake commercial advertising that scripts real people or uses actors to impersonate documentary subjects. We decline projects that compromise independent observation, and we refuse stories where informed, voluntary participant consent cannot be maintained throughout filming. Our studio does not produce promotional corporate films disguised as observational documentaries, nor do we film ungrounded or unverified claims. Every documentary commission requires complete creative integrity and direct access built upon mutual trust with our subjects.',
	'kea15b19a' => 'Night Shift at Ward Nine',
